Vendored third-party JavaScript/CSS. No file in this directory is fetched
at install time or runtime; integrity is enforced by SHA384SUMS
(verified by `scripts/check vendor` locally and in CI).

Current contents
----------------
xterm-5.3.0.js            xterm.js, legacy unscoped npm package `xterm`
xterm-5.3.0.css           (frozen at 5.3.0 since 2023)
xterm-addon-fit-0.8.0.js  legacy unscoped `xterm-addon-fit` (frozen at 0.8.0)

Provenance: these bytes were fetched from unpkg.com by the pre-refactor
install.sh (`xterm@latest` / `xterm-addon-fit@latest`) on 2026-01-31 and
have been serving the local web UI since. Versions are inferred from the
frozen legacy packages, not verified against npm — run
`scripts/vendor-update` to replace them with pinned, dual-CDN
cross-checked @xterm/xterm@5.5.0 + @xterm/addon-fit@0.10.0 (the
REFACTOR.md Phase 0 target), then update index.html references and this
file in the same commit.

Bumping a vendored file
-----------------------
1. Run `scripts/vendor-update` (or fetch the pinned file yourself).
2. Update SHA384SUMS in the same commit (`cd lib/ui/vendor && shasum -a 384 <files> > SHA384SUMS`).
3. Update references in lib/ui/index.html.
4. The diff — file rename + hash change — is reviewed like any other code.

socket.io-client is deliberately NOT vendored: Phase 1 replaces
flask_socketio with a hand-rolled RFC 6455 WebSocket and the client uses
the browser-native WebSocket API (see ARCHITECTURE.md §8).
